      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.loespejo.cl/historia/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 1857 construction of the Santiago‑Melipilla railway line brought the first station to Lo Espejo, sparking modest settlement around it.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lo_espejo",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "From the 1940s onward, CORVI housing projects and spontaneous land occupations on estates like Fundo Lo Sierra fueled Lo Espejo’s rapid urban growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/lo_espejo",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In May 1991, President Patricio Aylwin signed a decree that officially created the Municipality of Lo Espejo.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.loespejo.cl/historia/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "During the 1960s and 1970s, informal settlements such as José María Caro, Santa Adriana, and Clara Estrella emerged, shaping Lo Espejo’s modern landscape.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        24,
        25,
